        Mission Statement The Portsmouth Canvassing Authority is responsible for conducting all elections in the Town of Portsmouth. Under the direction of the State Board of Elections and in cooperation with the Secretary of State, the authority is involved in all phases of the electoral process, from voter registration to tallying the votes after the polls close on Election Day.There are approximately 15,074 registered voters in the Town of Portsmouth.Portsmouth Board of CanvassersThe Board of Canvassers is comprised of three bipartisan members who are appointed for 6-year terms by the Town Council and the Registrar of Voters is appointed by the Board of Canvassers. Two alternate members from each political party are also appointed by the Town Council.See the members serving on the Board of Canvassers.2022 Precinct Locations & MapThe new precinct map reflects the 2022 RI Redistricting Legislation signed into law on February 2022. Click to see map Portsmouth_VTDS_11x17 (1)IMPORTANT NOTE: The Portsmouth Multipurpose Senior Center and Melville Elementary School are no longer used as voting precincts. NO VOTING will occur at these locations on Election Day.The precincts below reflect the 2022 Redistricting Legislation passed by the RI General Assembly in February 2022.If you do not know your precinct, go vote.ri.gov to view your voter records and obtain a sample ballot.Portsmouth precincts open on Election Day 7AM and close at 8PM.NOTE: Some precincts may be combined for Primary Elections. Voters must verify locations before going to the polls on Election Day.2701 Hope Brown Center at Farnham Farm, 113 Mt Pleasant Ave., Prudence Island2702 CFP Arts, Wellness & Community Center, 933 Anthony Road2703 Portsmouth High School Field House NEW, 120 Education Lane2704 Portsmouth Friends Church NEW, 11 Middle Road2705 Portsmouth Town Council Chambers, 2200 East Main Road2706 St. Barnabas Parish Hall, 1697 East Main Road2707 Portsmouth Middle School Gymnasium, 125 Jepson Lane2708 Portsmouth Town Hall-- Limited Ballot, 2200 East Main Road2709 Portsmouth Town Hall (2nd Floor)--President/Vice- President ONLY Ballot, 2200 East Main RoadElected Officialshttp://sos.ri.gov/govdirectory/ to find elected officials. ElectionsPast Election ResultsFor official results go to Previous Election Results- Board of Elections (ri.gov)Upcoming Elections For upcoming election information go to https://vote.sos.ri.gov/Voter InformationTo obtain your voter information, go to the RI Department of State Voter Information Center online at https://vote.sos.ri.gov/ or call canvassing at 401-683-3157.
    


